<title>UK: L-Bank unit prices $500 million five-year bond.</title>
<headline>L-Bank unit prices $500 million five-year bond.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-04-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>The following bond has been priced, joint lead managers Goldman Sachs International and Morgan Stanley International said on Thursday.</p>
<p> BORROWER   BADEN-WUERTTEMBERG L-FINANCE</p>
<p> GUARANTOR  L-BANK</p>
<p> AMT	  $500 MLN  COUPON     7.00	MATURITY    30.APR.02</p>
<p> TYPE	 STRAIGHT  ISS PRICE  101.742   PAY DATE    30.APR.97</p>
<p> FULL FEES  1.875     REOFFER    100.117   SPREAD	+10 BP</p>
<p> MOODY	AAA	 LISTING    LUX	 PAY FREQ    ANNUAL</p>
<p> S&amp;P	  AAA	 DENOMS (K) 1-10-100  SALE LIMS US/GB/DE/NL</p>
<p> NEG PLG    NO	  CRS DEFLT  NO	  FORCE MAJ   IPMA 1</p>
<p> GOV LAW    GERMAN    HOME CTRY  GERMANY   TAX PROVS   STANDARD</p>
<p> MGT/UND    0.25	SELL CONC  1.625     PRAECIPUUM  NONE</p>
<p>UNDERLYING GOVT BOND 6.625 PCT U.S. T-NOTE DUE 31.MAR.02 -- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7658</p>
</text>
